	(text "Idrive setting:\n\n* Target rise time of 100ns-~1% of PWM period (~300ns).\n* Q_gd=5.0nC\n* Min = 5nC/300ns = 16mA\n* Max = 5nC/100ns = 50mA\n* 45mA source => 18kOhm R to AGND\n\nOver-current monitor:\n\n* Imax = 2 * Imax_motor = 32A\n* Rds(on)max = 8mOhm\n* Vds_ocp >= Imax * Rds(on)max = .256\n* Choose 0.4V => 75kOhm R to AGND\n\n* Sense Amp Gain:\n* Psense > Irms^2 * R\n* rms of 16A ~ 11.3\n* 2W shunt resistors are readily available\n* 2 > 11.3^2 * R => R < 15.6mOhm\n* Vo = (Vvref - 0.25V) - Vvref/2 = 1.4V\n* R = V_O / (A_V * I) :: .015 >= 1.4 / (A_V * 16A) => A_V <= 5.83\n* So we could use a gain of 5 if we wanted to dissipate two\n  watts at peak current.\n* However, to make it so that programming errors don't destroy\n  our board, we will use a weaker resistor and a gain of 10.\n* Doubling the gain halves our maximum resistance. We must\n  Stay *under* 7.5mOhm.\n* Gain of 10 = 45kOhm R to AGND.\n\n* Mode\n* 3PWM = 47kOhm R to AGND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "41e7fff1-dbc7-4542-a797-d6b0922b6009")
	)
